  "summary": "Possible namespace impersonation of @solana/web3.js",
  "details": "Package name `@solana-labs/web3js` closely resembles the legitimate `@solana/web3.js` Solana JavaScript SDK (different scope, missing dot in module name). The bundled `lib/index.cjs.js` and `lib/index.esm.js` contain the network and HTTP primitives expected of a Solana RPC client (fetch/POST for JSON-RPC, https.get, ping references for connection health), so keyword co-occurrence in the bundle alone cannot distinguish a legitimate Solana SDK from a lookalike with hidden harm. Name-similarity to a top-tier SDK warrants human review of publisher identity, source-to-bundle correspondence, and any divergence from the upstream `@solana/web3.js` API surface before a public block disposition.",
